contentText:
A couple got engaged at J. Cole&#8217;s The Fall-Off World Tour concert on Tuesday night (July 14) in Miami, and the Dreamville rapper made sure to show them some love during the show.

The fan got down on one knee during The Fall-Off &#8216;s &#8220;Life Sentence,&#8221; and his girlfriend was overcome with emotion before saying yes, which caused a stir in the section as fans cheered and took videos of the special moment.

Cole eventually became aware of the scene taking place, and he instructed the venue&#8217;s lights team to put the couple on the Jumbotron and spotlight them for the audience to see.

&#8220;That was amazing. Crowd, teamwork,&#8221; the 41-year-old said while processing what happened. &#8220;She said yes. Put the spotlight on my people back there that just got f&#8211;king proposed to [during] ‘Life Sentence.’ Oh my God. Spotlight team, whatever the f&#8211;k you did last time to whip that spotlight around.&#8221;

The camera crew eventually got the couple highlighted for the rest of the crowd to see and congratulate them, which included some words from Cole.

&#8220;Y&#8217;all see &#8217;em? What’s up, baby girl? What’s up, my boy? God bless y’all,&#8221; Cole said. &#8220;That’s f&#8211;king beautiful. Y’all make some noise for them, man.&#8221;

Love was certainly in the air of the Kaseya Center that night. Another couple revealed they were getting married on Wednesday (July 15) in Miami, and had their seats upgraded to the front row by Cole and his manager, Ibrahim Hamad.

The pair even got Cole&#8217;s attention during the show, also during the same song. &#8220;Y&#8217;all are getting married tomorrow? Oh my God! Y&#8217;all make some noise for my people in the front row who are getting married tomorrow,&#8221; Cole said. &#8220;Yeah, that&#8217;s who that song is for.&#8221;

&#8220;Aye @KingOfQueenz @JColeNC we just wanna say thank you for tonight’s show in Miami. our original tickets had an &#8216;obstructed view&#8217; and so y’all upgraded our tickets to the front row,&#8221; the fan wrote to X , and extended a wedding invite to Cole and IB. &#8220;Y’all let a bunch of fans since 2010 make a core memory. thank you. my lady and I get married tomorrow at 3pm in Miami if y’all would like to come. shoutout to Cole for showing us love during Life Sentence.&#8221;

J. Cole is currently on the road for The Fall-Off World Tour, which kicked off in Charlotte, N.C., on July 10. He&#8217;ll continue the trek this week with shows in Tampa Bay, Fla., and Atlanta.

Billed as Cole&#8217;s final album, The Fall-Off arrived in February and debuted atop the Billboard 200 with 280,000 total album-equivalent units earned, according to Luminate.
